[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Work Queues
PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-19-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Work Items

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-5
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Work item initialization
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to initialize a work item with a handler
function to be invoked when the item is processed.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to defer execution of a function to a thread context,
for example from an ISR, without creating a dedicated thread for each deferred operation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-6
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Static work item definition
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to define and initialize a work item at
compile time.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Submit work item to the system work queue
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to submit a work item for execution on the
system work queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Submit work item to a specific work queue
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to submit a work item for execution on a
caller-specified work queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Cancel a pending work item
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to cancel a work item that has been submitted
but not yet started, preventing its handler from being invoked.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Flush a work item
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to block until a submitted work item has
finished executing.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Query work item pending state
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to query whether a work item is currently
pending execution or running.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Delayable Work Items

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Delayable work item initialization
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to initialize a delayable work item with a
handler function, allowing it to be scheduled for execution after a specified delay.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-13
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Static delayable work item definition
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to define and initialize a delayable work item
at compile time.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-14
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Schedule a delayable work item
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to schedule a delayable work item to be
submitted to the system work queue after a specified timeout, if the item is not already
scheduled.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-15
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Schedule a delayable work item on a specific queue
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to schedule a delayable work item to be
submitted to a caller-specified work queue after a specified timeout.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-16
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Reschedule a delayable work item
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to reschedule a delayable work item,
replacing any existing scheduled delay with a new timeout value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-17
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Cancel a delayable work item
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to cancel a scheduled delayable work item
before it is submitted to a work queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-18
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Query remaining delay of a delayable work item
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to query the remaining time in system ticks
before a scheduled delayable work item is submitted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Work Queue Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-19
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: User-defined work queue initialization
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to initialize a user-defined work queue using
a caller-supplied thread stack, thread priority, and optional configuration.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to create a dedicated work queue thread with a specific
priority and stack size, separate from the system work queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-20
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: System work queue
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a pre-initialized system work queue available for general
use by kernel subsystems and applications.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-21
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Work queue drain
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to drain a work queue, blocking until all
currently pending work items have been processed and optionally preventing new items
from being submitted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-22
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Cancel work item and wait for completion
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to cancel a submitted work item and block
until any in-progress execution of that item's handler has completed, ensuring the
handler is not running when the call returns.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-23
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Flush a delayable work item
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to block until a delayable work item that
has been submitted to a work queue has finished executing its handler.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-24
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Cancel delayable work item and wait for completion
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to cancel a scheduled or submitted delayable
work item and block until any in-progress execution of that item's handler has completed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-19-25
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Stop a user work queue
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to stop a user-defined work queue, draining
pending work items and terminating the work queue thread, optionally waiting for
termination to complete before returning.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-33

[[/SECTION]]
